## 12:10 Carry the Explanation Forward

We can now answer the central question. Inspect the unchanged source to reveal its marks and identities; then choose purpose-dependent rules, apply each operation, and test the result with changed text.

Identification tells us what is present. Preparation applies our purpose-dependent decisions.

```text
source
→ inspect
→ identify relevant differences
→ choose rules for the purpose
→ apply and test those rules
→ prepared text
```

Do not make the common mistake of treating every real difference as one that should disappear. A difference may be meaningful, and purpose decides whether we preserve it.

When new source arrives, the same sequence lets you explain and predict its result. Prepared text is now the dependable building block for the next lesson.
